attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a long spine.** Columns 0 to 28, `pgl` to `cydA`, are carried by 92 to 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 2 to 7% of calls {S1}. The model names 95 to 99% of them, fewest at column 26, `cydX`, 95% {S1}.

@variable **A fork follows at columns 29 to 31**, carried by 28 to 62%, all shell, the stretch most in regions of plasticity, 51 to 52% {S2, P}. A second branch of 3 families runs through those columns in 23 to 24%, `hypothetical protein` to `glmS` {S2.b29}. Then the `sdh` genes, columns 36 to 39, [[succinate dehydrogenase]], and the `ybg` genes, columns 42 to 45, [[fimbrial biogenesis]] {S3, S4, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine columns than on the fork and variable ones**, 96 against 89%, and hesitates less there, 0.21 against 0.54 bits {M}. It hesitates most at column 29, a fork column, 1.98 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on fork and variable columns.** Columns 62 to 79, `kdpC` to `glnS`, are carried by 31 to 89%, 13 persistent and 5 shell {S8}. The last column is `glnS`, in 46% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 94% of genes**, 0.32 bits on average, perplexity 1.4 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.00 against 0.18 bits, and names fewer genes, 77% against 97% {C}.

